<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
    Access tier for internal coaches. Assign to selected colleagues only; the admin
    tier is the org profile, not a permission set.

    Object rights and the fieldPermissions are derived from the GraphQL operations
    the UI bundle actually issues (Create/Update/Delete mutations and the field
    selections of `uiapi { query }`). Consequences worth knowing:

    - AuditEvent__c gets Create but no Update. The app writes audit events in the
      acting user's own UI API session, so without Create every audit write fails
      with INSUFFICIENT_ACCESS. Update stays off because the log is append-only.
    - AuditEvent__c needs viewAllRecords: it is the one object whose internal
      org-wide default is Private. View All bypasses that, where changing the OWD
      would have been a global change instead of a revocable assignment.
    - Participant__c and Program__c have no Delete; the bundle issues no delete
      mutation for either.
    - Coach_Profile__c is read-only. Appointment__c.Coach__c is a lookup to User,
      not to Coach_Profile__c (see src/api/user/userService.ts).

    31 required fields are deliberately absent from fieldPermissions.
    Salesforce rejects any fieldPermissions entry for a required field
    ("You cannot deploy to a required field"), and none of the 29 permission sets
    in the org lists one either. Their field-level security therefore comes from
    the assigned profile: see docs/coach-access.md before assigning this set.
-->
